# drover daily-pull cron template
#
# Pulls yesterday's Acquia application error logs into the project's
# canonical folder. Place this file (or its content) into your crontab
# via `crontab -e`. Adjust DROVER_PROJECT_ROOT, DROVER_PULL_PY, and the
# log destination to match your machine.
#
# Why 02:30 UTC: Acquia rotates logs at midnight UTC. A 2.5-hour buffer
# is enough for snapshot-generation latency without crowding the
# rotation window itself.
#
# Why --env all: pulls every env listed in the manifest (typically prod,
# stage, dev). Reports can later filter to whichever env they want.
#
# Why --daily: only pulls yesterday — already-present days short-circuit.
# Use a separate `--backfill` cron weekly if you want gap recovery on
# top of the daily nominal pull.
#
# Test the line locally first:
#   $DROVER_PYTHON $DROVER_PULL_PY --project $DROVER_PROJECT_ROOT --env all --daily
#
# Failure handling: the script exits non-zero on any unrecovered failure.
# Pair with `mailto` or your alert tool to be paged when a day fails.

DROVER_PYTHON=/usr/bin/python3
DROVER_PROJECT_ROOT=/path/to/your/project
DROVER_PULL_PY=/path/to/.claude/plugins/cache/local/drover/<version>/scripts/pull.py
DROVER_LOG=/var/log/drover/pull.log

# m   h    dom mon dow  command
30   2    *   *   *    $DROVER_PYTHON $DROVER_PULL_PY --project $DROVER_PROJECT_ROOT --env all --daily >> $DROVER_LOG 2>&1

# Weekly backfill — catches any days the daily pull missed
0    3    *   *   0    $DROVER_PYTHON $DROVER_PULL_PY --project $DROVER_PROJECT_ROOT --env all --backfill >> $DROVER_LOG 2>&1
